  "dependency_review": "Inspected the intake row (notion_id 3b431704-6eeb-81d6-bd9f-f78648da71de, recording 2026-09-21 14-25-45, lane 'diagram build', topic 'Hermes Agent now reads your PDFs and documents 100% locally, without a single API call, using AnyDoc, the open-source PDF analyzer built by the Firecrawl team'), the approved plan, scene handoff, cutout and whiteboard notes, and the TITLE constant of the approved split generator ('Hermes Agent reads your documents locally'), which the split and cutout index.html titles carry and is the package title; the Notion idea ID is the short_id. The three editable projects each carry index.html; every local src/href resolves inside its tree, and the whiteboard's assets folder is a symlink into stage/hermesdocs_whiteboard that delivery materializes as real files. Generators: hermesdocs_scene.py, the split, cutout (plus envelope) and whiteboard generators and _hermesdocs_proof.py; their imports resolve to pipeline/captions.py, pipeline/pointing_cues.py, formats/cutout/lib (cutout_core, cutout_depthfield) and formats/whiteboard/lib (whiteboard_build, whiteboard_fix6_core), all included; the rest is stdlib, numpy and PIL. Media and timing: the raw recording, its full Scribe transcript, the whole cuts/hermesdocs set (master, face plates, audio, EDL, tight transcript) and the seven prep stage records. Matting: the matting/hermesdocs session (selection with Astra edits, v5 alpha/cut/rim layers, plates, prompts, chair audit, ship record, cache); no matting_fallback session exists for this Short. Config and paperwork: every gen/_*hermesdocs* build, BiRefNet master, cue, envelope, gate, geometry, prerender, pill-width, QC, render-control, spec and whiteboard record. Review: final_hermesdocs.json (Miguel's approval on the staged videos), agent start/done/state records, the Astra matte prompt, log and result, matte reviews, proof crops, sheets and the legacy phone records; the Astra pid file is excluded as runtime state. External runtime dependencies recorded, not vendored: GSAP 3.14.2 from jsDelivr and Google Fonts at render time, HyperFrames CLI, Playwright Chromium and ffmpeg. No secrets and no other Short's files.",
